# Isolated offsite restore rehearsal. Copy to a chmod-600 gitignored file.
# Do not reuse the live artifact-store (MinIO) keys.
#
# Preferred already-configured mapping (Cloudflare R2):
#   source .merc-secrets.env and let scripts/offsite-independent-restore.sh
#   map R2_ENDPOINT / R2_BUCKET / R2_* keys onto these names.
#
# MERC_BACKUP_OFFSITE=s3://your-bucket/offsite-alpha
# MERC_BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://<accountid>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# MERC_BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_RECIPIENT=age1...
# MERC_BACKUP_DECRYPTION_IDENTITY_FILE=/absolute/path/to/mode-0600-age-identity
#
# Isolated rehearsal (`make offsite-independent-restore`) mints a throwaway
# age identity, uploads only ciphertext, destroys that source, then
# downloads and restores into a second isolated compose.
#
# Live droplet backup (`make offsite-droplet-restore`) encrypts on the
# droplet against MERC_BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_RECIPIENT or a persistent
# ~/.merc/offsite-age-identity, uploads only ciphertext, and never
# targets merc-postgres-1 or the merc_pgdata volume for restore.
